cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QuantumNovelty in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "QuantumNovelty: an audit-and-falsify framework for quantum-computing research papers and patents"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kashani"
    given-names: "Shlomo"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BoltzmannEntropy/QuantumNovelty"
url: "https://boltzmannentropy.github.io/QuantumNovelty.github.io/"
abstract: >-
  Agent-skill framework for writing and reviewing quantum-computing
  papers and examining quantum patents: a 5-voice referee panel and a
  6-voice simulated USPTO examiner panel (35 U.S.C. §§ 101/102/103/112 →
  an Office Action), each with a deterministic quality gate, an 11-fallacy
  quantum-CS taxonomy, strict-domination novelty audits, and an exact
  token + USD cost ledger on every LLM call. Runs on the Claude Code CLI
  by default.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - peer review
  - patent examination
  - USPTO office action
  - LLM agents
  - research automation
  - novelty audit
